From a10ef3ec90cc59332cd09c87e37588327ef05d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devon Jonte <devonjonte@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:04:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] offset_check.py: ten candidates a cell rescanned; 8 of 8
 runs detect on the i7

The three misses of 9145354 were selection: one quick reading strays as
high as a slow state reads, and the window's offsets ranked anywhere
from 1st to 10th of 256 under readings that read 0.73 again when
rescanned. Rescanning each cell's ten worst (a rescan run takes a
fraction of a second): 8 of 8 runs exit 0 on the i7-12700K (servil
2e892e1: 5 of 5; 082afa3: 3 of 3), about 97 s each, no batch cell ever
judged sensitive. Found: shared lent 64 B at thread stack +3472..+3520
in 7 runs, shared continuous 64 B at +912..+960 in 6.
---
 tools/offset_check.py | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/offset_check.py b/tools/offset_check.py
index 312d72f..d23c956 100644
--- a/tools/offset_check.py
