Subject: [PATCH 5/5] offset_check.py: our 64-byte hash() immune; the upstream
 crate's is the control

With the chunk-root kernel our hash() of 64 bytes keeps off the stack and
shows no window at any offset (#141); it moves to IMMUNE_CELLS. The check
still needs cells it knows to be sensitive, on every machine: the upstream
blake3 crate's 64-byte hash() keeps its chunk state on the stack as ours
did, so it is measured beside ours and its cells are the controls.
